<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador Jan trade deficit $9 mln v $15 mln surplus.</title>
<headline>Ecuador Jan trade deficit $9 mln v $15 mln surplus.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador posted a trade deficit of $9 million in January, down from a $15 million surplus in the same month last year, the Central Bank said Thursday.</p>
<p>Exports reached $371 million, up from $362 million in January 1996. Imports grew to $380 million from $347 million.</p>
<p>Ecuador had a trade surplus of $1.37 billion for 1996, up from a $354 million surplus in 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
